during the Second World War there were  many resistance movements across Europe  who refused to accept their country's  occupations the most famous is of course  the French Resistance but one resistance  movement which doesn't get too much  attention is the Yugoslav one it was a  movement which fought for Yugoslavian  dependents and inflicted major damage on  their occupiers Yugoslavia was also one  of the only nations in the water mostly  liberate themselves this raises the  question why were they so effective in a  twist of events the Yugoslav resistance  was fractured and so to get a better  view of things some backstory is  necessary by the time the war started  Yugoslavia was a relatively new country  having been created after World War one  and the collapse of the austro-hungarian  Empire it was a multi-ethnic Kingdom  whose government was for the most part  dominated by Serbians who were the  largest ethnic group ethnic tensions  were a grave concern to the ruling  government in the monarch King Peter ii  who wasn't of age yet and so Yugoslavia  was governed by a regent Prince Paul  Paul was growing ever more concerned  about Germany and particularly Italy who  had designs on Yugoslavian land and also  had just eaten Albania Paul wanted to  stay neutral and protect Yugoslavian  independence but his government was  largely Pro Ally  by early 1941 the Allies weren't exactly  doing well and so Paul agreed to sign  the tripartite pact but as a neutral  nation the Yugoslav people are many in  the military were fiercely anti German  and so this action was followed by  protests and in late March Paul was  ousted in a coup this coup placed Peter  in charge with an even more Pro British  government in roughly two weeks later  the axis invaded and swiftly conquered  the country  it was then divided between the Axis  powers like this this part here was  called the independent state of Croatia  because it was a puppet state run by  Crowe arts in fact it was run by a  fascist group called the estar J who  probably carried out ethnic cleansing in  its new territories whilst the country  itself had formally surrendered this  didn't mean that everyone who lived  there accepted it so there were two main  groups of resistors the first were the  Chetniks which was the serbian royalist  movement led by drazi Mikhaylovich the  second were the most famous the  partisans who were a multi-ethnic  communist movement that by Joseph  brought Tito which was founded after  Germany invaded the USSR at first the  two groups work together to sabotage the  axis but ideological differences eroded  away any trust that they had the  Chetniks who were basically the remnants  of the Yugoslav army took the role of  selective collaboration and the plan was  to wait for the Allies to come to their  aid this led to them simply waiting for  the axis to leave and given the  hostility to the  - or them eventually receive material  aid from Italy as for the communist  partisans they'd have sooner died than  collaborate and were based on a corps of  veterans from the Spanish Civil War they  conducted sabotage raided supplies  attack soldiers and routinely liberated  areas from the axis in fact the  partisans were such a problem that the  axis had to maintain over 100,000  soldiers in Yugoslavia to deal with them  resistance continued to grow throughout  the war and in 1943 the Allies  recognized the partisans as the  legitimate resistance and not the  Chetniks by this point the partisans had  over a quarter of a million people in  its service one reason for this was that  it was a Yugoslav movement not a Sur B  one and also because tito gave amnesty  several times to those who had supported  the Chetniks or the axis which boosted  the partisans greatly and this is  ultimately what led to their success the  people of Yugoslavia had disliked the  Germans and the ruling Serbian classes  before the war and the Yugoslav  communists were neva tito was a clever  leader who knew how to get people on  board with the unified vision of the  future  they were also based in the mountainous  regions of Yugoslavia from which they  were extremely hard to dislodge and it  was all of these things combined which  made them so effective and ultimately  led to Yugoslavia being a constant thorn  in the axis side I hope you enjoyed this  episode and thank you for watching with  extra thanks to my patreon supporters  which you can see on screen and with an  extra special thanks to James  Bissonnette David archaeologist Ozark a  flash Party Boyko Rob Waterhouse Chris  wicker Michael Reynolds Gustav Swann  David Silverman spinning three plates  Maggie packs Kowski Christian check'  Anthony Beckett Ike Skye Chappell and  Winston K wood  you
 

